er the d’Alembert differential equation\n\n$$\ny=x(1+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})+\\frac{3}{2}{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{2}-\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nIf ${y}^{′}(x)=t,$ then general solution can be expressed in parametric form $(x(t),y(t)),$ where\n\n$$\nx(t)=C{e}^{-t}+f(t)\n$$\n\nand $C$ is an arbitrary constant. Find the function $f(t).$\n\n*Hint: Under the given transformation, we have*\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+x=1-3t.\n$$\n\n*You may also wish to make use of the following result (constants omitted):*\n\n$$\n\\int t{e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t=(t-1){e}^{t}\n$$" 13194139535236 true] [17592186339071 1113 #uuid "e9151b70-2cb0-5312-ba19-ff72c23b0f47" 13194139535236 true] [17592186339071 1145 "A differential equation is a d'Alembert differential equation if it can be expressed in the form\n\n$$\ny=xf({y}^{′})+g({y}^{′}),\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are differentiable functions of ${y}^{′}.$ \n\nWe're told that, under the substitution ${y}^{′}(x)=t,$ our d’Alembert differential equation transforms to the first-order linear equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+x=1-3t.\n$$\n\nWe'll solve this equation using the method of integrating factors. Since this equation is already of the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+P(t)x=Q(t)\n$$\n\nwe compute our integrating factor as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(t) & ={e}^{\\int P(t)\\,\\text{d}t}={e}^{\\int 1\\,\\text{d}t}={e}^{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying our differential equation by $I(t)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+x{e}^{t} & =(1-3t){e}^{t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRewriting the left-hand side as an exact derivative, and integrating both sides of the equation with respect to $t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(x{e}^{t}) & =(1-3t){e}^{t} \\\\ \\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(x{e}^{t})\\,\\text{d}t & =\\int (1-3t){e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ x{e}^{t} & =\\int (1-3t){e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ x{e}^{t} & =\\int {e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t-3\\int t{e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ x{e}^{t} & ={e}^{t}-3(t-1){e}^{t}+C \\\\ x & =4-3t+C{e}^{-t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that\n\n$$\nx(t)=C{e}^{-t}+4-3t\n$$\n\nand finally, $f(t)=4-3t.$" 13194139535236 true] [17592186339072 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339073 13194139535236 true] [17592186339072 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339074 13194139535236 true] [17592186339072 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339075 13194139535236 true] [17592186339072 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339076 13194139535236 true] [17592186339072 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339077 13194139535236 true] [17592186339072 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535236 true] [17592186339072 1041 "selection" 13194139535236 true] [17592186339072 1104 #edb/ref 17592186339073 13194139535236 true] [17592186339072 1110 #uuid "2752a01b-5638-5477-8e4e-774be2937898" 13194139535236 true] [17592186339073 1034 "f(t)=4-3t" 13194139535236 true] [17592186339073 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535236 true] [17592186339073 1111 #uuid "30c20f35-ae3f-5da1-bb0c-f96b6c862d96" 13194139535236 true] [17592186339074 1034 "f(t)=4-t" 13194139535236 true] [17592186339074 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535236 true] [17592186339074 1111 #uuid "21a0589f-f6fe-56fb-9cbd-6f6facc6e6e5" 13194139535236 true] [17592186339075 1034 "f(t)=4+3t" 13194139535236 true] [17592186339075 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535236 true] [17592186339075 1111 #uuid "6e33fd0d-e752-50d1-ad81-d31d5112603d" 13194139535236 true] [17592186339076 1034 "f(t)=5-3t" 13194139535236 true] [17592186339076 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535236 true] [17592186339076 1111 #uuid "20c9c7a0-92cf-54b1-ba4c-b1baed0794be" 13194139535236 true] [17592186339077 1034 "f(t)=3-4t" 13194139535236 true] [17592186339077 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535236 true] [17592186339077 1111 #uuid "64734250-da3c-5d28-9449-083df2e2ad4f" 13194139535236 true] [17592186339078 1017 #edb/ref 17592186339079 13194139535236 true] [17592186339078 1089 "q-337721" 13194139535236 true] [1759