{e}^{\\int P(t)\\,\\text{d}t} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int \\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}t} \\\\  & ={e}^{t/2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying our differential equation by $I(t)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t/2}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{1}{2}x{e}^{t/2} & =t{e}^{t/2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRewriting the left-hand side as an exact derivative, and integrating both sides of the equation with respect to $t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(x{e}^{t/2}) & =t{e}^{t/2} \\\\ \\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(x{e}^{t/2})\\,\\text{d}t & =\\int t{e}^{t/2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ x{e}^{t/2} & =(2t-4){e}^{t/2}+C \\\\ x & =2t-4+C{e}^{-t/2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that\n\n$$\nx(t)=C{e}^{-t/2}+2t-4.\n$$\n\nTo recover $y$, we substitute $x$ into\n\n$$\ny=x(t+2)-{t}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(t) & =(C{e}^{-t/2}+2t-4)(t+2)-{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we conclude that $f(t)=t+2,\\text{ }g(t)=-{t}^{2},$ and\n\n$$\nf(t)+g(t)=-{t}^{2}+t+2.\n$$" 13194139535236 true] [17592186339086 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339087 13194139535236 true] [17592186339086 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339088 13194139535236 true] [17592186339086 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339089 13194139535236 true] [17592186339086 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339090 13194139535236 true] [17592186339086 1000 #edb/ref 17592186339091 13194139535236 true] [17592186339086 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535236 true] [17592186339086 1041 "selection" 13194139535236 true] [17592186339086 1104 #edb/ref 17592186339089 13194139535236 true] [17592186339086 1110 #uuid "884136c1-0552-5e75-a8ab-27e04fb189ff" 13194139535236 true] [17592186339087 1034 "{t}^{2}-t-2" 13194139535236 true] [17592186339087 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535236 true] [17592186339087 1111 #uuid "bcc3e7b4-34b2-52db-b638-548c3e47a758" 13194139535236 true] [17592186339088 1034 "-{t}^{2}+t-2" 13194139535236 true] [17592186339088 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535236 true] [17592186339088 1111 #uuid "f7b5